  "title": "Njinga of Ndongo and Matamba",
  "summary": "Njinga (also spelled Nzinga) ruled Ndongo and Matamba in what is now Angola. Sent to negotiate with the Portuguese at Luanda in 1622, she later resisted Portuguese expansion, fled to Matamba in 1626, allied with the Dutch after 1641 and signed a peace treaty in 1657. She also used the slave trade to fund her wars. She died in 1663.",
